</nav>


<!-- ==========================================
     HEADER
=========================================== -->

<div class="header">

    <h1>🟦 C++ Programming</h1>

    <p>
        Learn C++ programming for placement exams
    </p>

</div>


<div class="container mt-5 mb-5">


    <!-- ==========================================
         INTRODUCTION
    =========================================== -->

    <h2 class="text-center page-title">

        💻 C++ Programming

    </h2>

    <hr>


    <p>

        C++ is a powerful object-oriented programming language
        widely used in technical interviews and placement exams.
        It supports procedural programming, object-oriented
        programming, templates, STL, and competitive programming.

    </p>


    <!-- ==========================================
         TOPICS COVERED
    =========================================== -->

    <h4 class="mt-4">

        📚 Topics Covered

    </h4>


    <ul class="list-group mb-4">

        <li class="list-group-item">
            Basic C++ Program
        </li>

        <li class="list-group-item">
            Variables and Data Types
        </li>

        <li class="list-group-item">
            Input and Output
        </li>

        <li class="list-group-item">
            Operators
        </li>

        <li class="list-group-item">
            If-Else Statements
        </li>

        <li class="list-group-item">
            Loops
        </li>

        <li class="list-group-item">
            Arrays
        </li>

        <li class="list-group-item">
            Strings
        </li>

        <li class="list-group-item">
            Functions
        </li>

        <li class="list-group-item">
            Pointers
        </li>

        <li class="list-group-item">
            Object-Oriented Programming
        </li>

        <li class="list-group-item">
            STL
        </li>

    </ul>


    <!-- ==========================================
         TOPIC DEFINITIONS
    =========================================== -->

    <h4>

        📖 C++ Topic Definitions

    </h4>


    <div class="accordion"
         id="cppTopics">


        <!-- BASIC PROGRAM -->

        <div class="accordion-item">

            <h2 class="accordion-header">

                <button
                    class="accordion-button collapsed"
                    data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#basicTopic">

                    1. Basic C++ Program

                </button>

            </h2>


            <div
                id="basicTopic"
                class="accordion-collapse collapse">

                <div class="accordion-body">

                    Every C++ program starts execution from
                    the <strong>main()</strong> function.

<pre>#include &lt;iostream&gt;
using namespace std;

int main() {

    cout &lt;&lt; "Hello World";

    return 0;
}</pre>

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>


        <!-- VARIABLES -->

        <div class="accordion-item">

            <h2 class="accordion-header">

                <button
                    class="accordion-button collapsed"
                    data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#variablesTopic">

                    2. Variables and Data Types

                </button>

            </h2>


            <div
                id="variablesTopic"
                class="accordion-collapse collapse">

                <div class="accordion-body">

                    Variables store data values.

                    <ul>

                        <li>
                            int – Integer values
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            float – Decimal values
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            char – Character
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            double – Large decimal values
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            bool – True or false
                        </li>

                    </ul>

<pre>int age = 20;

float marks = 85.5;

char grade = 'A';

bool passed = true;</pre>

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>


        <!-- INPUT OUTPUT -->

        <div class="accordion-item">

            <h2 class="accordion-header">

                <button
                    class="accordion-button collapsed"
                    data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#inputTopic">

                    3. Input and Output

                </button>

            </h2>


            <div
                id="inputTopic"
                class="accordion-collapse collapse">

                <div class="accordion-body">

                    C++ uses <strong>cin</strong> for input and
                    <strong>cout</strong> for output.

<pre>int age;

cin &gt;&gt; age;

cout &lt;&lt; "Age = " &lt;&lt; age;</pre>

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>


        <!-- IF ELSE -->

        <div class="accordion-item">

            <h2 class="accordion-header">

                <button
                    class="accordion-button collapsed"
                    data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#ifTopic">

                    4. If-Else

                </button>

            </h2>


            <div
                id="ifTopic"
                class="accordion-collapse collapse">

                <div class="accordion-body">

                    If-else is used to make decisions.

<pre>int age = 20;

if(age &gt;= 18) {

    cout &lt;&lt; "Eligible";

}
else {

    cout &lt;&lt; "Not Eligible";

}</pre>

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>


        <!-- LOOPS -->

        <div class="accordion-item">

            <h2 class="accordion-header">

                <button
                    class="accordion-button collapsed"
                    data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#loopTopic">

                    5. Loops

                </button>

            </h2>


            <div
                id="loopTopic"
                class="accordion-collapse collapse">

                <div class="accordion-body">

                    Loops execute a block of code repeatedly.

<pre>for(int i = 1; i &lt;= 5; i++) {

    cout &lt;&lt; i &lt;&lt; " ";

}</pre>

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>


        <!-- ARRAYS -->

        <div class="accordion-item">

            <h2 class="accordion-header">

                <button
                    class="accordion-button collapsed"
                    data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#arrayTopic">

                    6. Arrays

                </button>

            </h2>


            <div
                id="arrayTopic"
                class="accordion-collapse collapse">

                <div class="accordion-body">

                    Arrays store multiple values of the same
                    data type.

<pre>int numbers[5] =
{10, 20, 30, 40, 50};

cout &lt;&lt; numbers[0];</pre>

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>


        <!-- FUNCTIONS -->

        <div class="accordion-item">

            <h2 class="accordion-header">

                <button
                    class="accordion-button collapsed"
                    data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#functionTopic">

                    7. Functions

                </button>

            </h2>


            <div
                id="functionTopic"
                class="accordion-collapse collapse">

                <div class="accordion-body">

                    Functions are reusable blocks of code.

<pre>int add(int a, int b) {

    return a + b;

}</pre>

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>


        <!-- OOPS -->

        <div class="accordion-item">

            <h2 class="accordion-header">

                <button
                    class="accordion-button collapsed"
                    data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#oopsTopic">

                    8. Object-Oriented Programming

                </button>

            </h2>


            <div
                id="oopsTopic"
                class="accordion-collapse collapse">

                <div class="accordion-body">

                    C++ supports OOP concepts such as:

                    <ul>

                        <li>Class</li>

                        <li>Object</li>

                        <li>Inheritance</li>

                        <li>Polymorphism</li>

                        <li>Encapsulation</li>

                        <li>Abstraction</li>

                    </ul>

<pre>class Student {

public:

    string name;

    void display() {

        cout &lt;&lt; name;

    }

};</pre>

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>


        <!-- STL -->

        <div class="accordion-item">

            <h2 class="accordion-header">

                <button
                    class="accordion-button collapsed"
                    data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#stlTopic">

                    9. STL

                </button>

            </h2>


            <div
                id="stlTopic"
                class="accordion-collapse collapse">

                <div class="accordion-body">

                    STL stands for Standard Template Library.
                    It provides useful data structures and
                    algorithms.

                    <ul>

                        <li>vector</li>

                        <li>stack</li>

                        <li>queue</li>

                        <li>set</li>

                        <li>map</li>

                        <li>sort()</li>

                    </ul>

<pre>#include &lt;vector&gt;

vector&lt;int&gt; numbers;

numbers.push_back(10);
numbers.push_back(20);</pre>

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- ==========================================
         PRACTICE QUESTIONS
    =========================================== -->

    <h4 class="mt-5">

        📝 C++ Practice Questions

    </h4>


    <!-- QUESTION 1 -->

    <div class="question-card">

        <div class="question-title">

            Question 1

        </div>

        <div class="question-text">

            Which function is the starting point of
            execution in a C++ program?

        </div>


        <label class="option">

            <input
                type="radio"
                name="q1"
                value="main">

            main()

        </label>


        <label class="option">

            <input
                type="radio"
                name="q1"
                value="start">

            start()

        </label>


        <label class="option">

            <input
                type="radio"
                name="q1"
                value="run">

            run()

        </label>


        <label class="option">

            <input
                type="radio"
                name="q1"
                value="execute">

            execute()

        </label>


        <button
            class="submit-question"
            onclick="checkAnswer(1, 'main')">

            Submit Answer

        </button>


        <div id="result1"
             class="answer-result"></div>

    </div>


    <!-- QUESTION 2 -->

    <div class="question-card">

        <div class="question-title">

            Question 2

        </div>

        <div class="question-text">

            Which operator is used with cout to display
            output in C++?

        </div>


        <label class="option">

            <input
                type="radio"
                name="q2"
                value=">>">

            &gt;&gt;

        </label>


        <label class="option">

            <input
                type="radio"
                name="q2"
                value="<<">

            &lt;&lt;

        </label>


        <label class="option">

            <input
                type="radio"
                name="q2"
                value="==">

            ==

        </label>


        <label class="option">

            <input
                type="radio"
                name="q2"
                value="=">

            =

        </label>


        <button
            class="submit-question"
            onclick="checkAnswer(2, '<<')">

            Submit Answer

        </button>


        <div id="result2"
             class="answer-result"></div>

    </div>


    <!-- QUESTION 3 -->

    <div class="question-card">

        <div class="question-title">

            Question 3

        </div>

        <div class="question-text">

            Which data type is used to store a single
            character?

        </div>


        <label class="option">

            <input
                type="radio"
                name="q3"
                value="int">

            int

        </label>


        <label class="option">

            <input
                type="radio"
                name="q3"
                value="float">

            float

        </label>


        <label class="option">

            <input
                type="radio"
                name="q3"
                value="char">

            char

        </label>


        <label class="option">

            <input
                type="radio"
                name="q3"
                value="string">

            string

        </label>


        <button
            class="submit-question"
            onclick="checkAnswer(3, 'char')">

            Submit Answer

        </button>


        <div id="result3"
             class="answer-result"></div>

    </div>


    <!-- QUESTION 4 -->

    <div class="question-card">

        <div class="question-title">

            Question 4

        </div>

        <div class="question-text">

            Which loop is commonly used when the number
            of iterations is known?

        </div>


        <label class="option">

            <input
                type="radio"
                name="q4"
                value="for">

            for loop

        </label>


        <label class="option">

            <input
                type="radio"
                name="q4"
                value="while">

            while loop

        </label>


        <label class="option">

            <input
                type="radio"
                name="q4"
                value="do">

            do-while loop

        </label>


        <label class="option">

            <input
                type="radio"
                name="q4"
                value="switch">

            switch

        </label>


        <button
            class="submit-question"
            onclick="checkAnswer(4, 'for')">

            Submit Answer

        </button>


        <div id="result4"
             class="answer-result"></div>

    </div>


    <!-- QUESTION 5 -->

    <div class="question-card">

        <div class="question-title">

            Question 5

        </div>

        <div class="question-text">

            What is the index of the first element
            in a C++ array?

        </div>


        <label class="option">

            <input
                type="radio"
                name="q5"
                value="0">

            0

        </label>


        <label class="option">

            <input
                type="radio"
                name="q5"
                value="1">

            1

        </label>


        <label class="option">

            <input
                type="radio"
                name="q5"
                value="-1">

            -1

        </label>


        <label class="option">

            <input
                type="radio"
                name="q5"
                value="2">

            2

        </label>


        <button
            class="submit-question"
            onclick="checkAnswer(5, '0')">

            Submit Answer

        </button>


        <div id="result5"
             class="answer-result"></div>

    </div>


    <!-- QUESTION 6 -->

    <div class="question-card">

        <div class="question-title">

            Question 6

        </div>

        <div class="question-text">

            Which concept allows a class to acquire
            properties of another class?

        </div>


        <label class="option">

            <input
                type="radio"
                name="q6"
                value="encapsulation">

            Encapsulation

        </label>


        <label class="option">

            <input
                type="radio"
                name="q6"
                value="inheritance">

            Inheritance

        </label>


        <label class="option">

            <input
                type="radio"
                name="q6"
                value="abstraction">

            Abstraction

        </label>


        <label class="option">

            <input
                type="radio"
                name="q6"
                value="overloading">

            Overloading

        </label>


        <button
            class="submit-question"
            onclick="checkAnswer(6, 'inheritance')">

            Submit Answer

        </button>


        <div id="result6"
             class="answer-result"></div>

    </div>


    <!-- QUESTION 7 -->

    <div class="question-card">

        <div class="question-title">

            Question 7

        </div>

        <div class="question-text">

            Which STL container stores elements in
            dynamic array form?

        </div>


        <label class="option">

            <input
                type="radio"
                name="q7"
                value="stack">

            stack

        </label>


        <label class="option">

            <input
                type="radio"
                name="q7"
                value="vector">

            vector

        </label>


        <label class="option">

            <input
                type="radio"
                name="q7"
                value="queue">

            queue

        </label>


        <label class="option">

            <input
                type="radio"
                name="q7"
                value="set">

            set

        </label>


        <button
            class="submit-question"
            onclick="checkAnswer(7, 'vector')">

            Submit Answer

        </button>


        <div id="result7"
             class="answer-result"></div>

    </div>


    <!-- QUESTION 8 -->

    <div class="question-card">

        <div class="question-title">

            Question 8

        </div>

        <div class="question-text">

            What will be the output?

<pre>int a = 10;
int b = 20;

cout &lt;&lt; a + b;</pre>

        </div>


        <label class="option">

            <input
                type="radio"
                name="q8"
                value="10">

            10

        </label>


        <label class="option">

            <input
                type="radio"
                name="q8"
                value="20">

            20

